---
/**
 * Coupling — third biology-lens concept at Interactive scale.
 * Sustained structural or functional link between living units.
 * Order: Signal → Recognition → Coupling. Completes Interactive; opens Collective.
 * Keep inline tags on one line with outer spaces (Astro whitespace).
 * No em-dashes in public copy.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Coupling | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="min-h-[50vh] flex flex-col justify-center pt-28 pb-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40 mb-6">
					Biology lens · Interactive Identity
				</div>
				<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-[0.95] mb-6 text-white">
					Coupling
				</h1>
				<p class="text-xl text-white/50 font-light leading-relaxed mb-6">
					A sustained structural or functional link between living units:
					more than a single signal, less than a fused identity.
				</p>
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-500/20 bg-amber-500/[0.04] p-4">
					<p class="text-sm text-white/65 leading-relaxed">
						<strong class="text-white/80">Status:</strong> Working concept under the biology lens.
						Primary science reading: cell junctions, adhesion, and stable intercellular coupling.
						Analogy, not isomorphism. Completes Interactive after
						<a href="/framework/signal" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Signal</a>
						and
						<a href="/framework/recognition" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Recognition</a>.
						Opens toward Collective (Multicellularity).
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Definition</div>
				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white">Relation that holds in time.</h2>
				<p>
					In biology, cells can form more than transient contacts.
					<strong class="text-white/85">Coupling</strong> names durable links: junctions, adhesion complexes, coordinated channels,
					stable neighborhoods in a tissue. The units remain distinct; the link persists and carries repeated exchange.
				</p>
				<p>
					In Identity Engineering, Coupling is the biology-lens name for that sustained interactive structure.
					After
					<a href="/framework/signal" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Signal</a>
					(event) and
					<a href="/framework/recognition" class="text-white/85 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Recognition</a>
					(admission logic), Coupling is what forms when exchange continues under maintained boundaries:
					a bond, a channel, a practiced relation — not yet a multicellular Collective Identity.
				</p>
				<p>
					Under the physics lens, interactive forces (Gravitation, Frequency, Relativity) describe pull and measurement between identities.
					Coupling is the living-form reading of a relation that stays online without erasing either Cell.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Coupling is</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Sustained link:</strong> structure or practice that outlasts a single signal event.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Preserved distinctness:</strong> two (or more) Cells remain separate forms with their own Boundaries and Stems.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Channel for repeated exchange:</strong> signals can flow under standing recognition, not only one-off encounters.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Bridge to Collective:</strong> when many couplings stabilize into a higher-order living system, Multicellularity becomes the next scale.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">What Coupling is not</div>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not a single Signal.</strong>
						An event can start a path to coupling; it is not yet the sustained link.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Recognition alone.</strong>
						Admission policy enables coupling; it does not constitute the bond.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not fusion or absorption.</strong>
						If one Identity dissolves into the other, Boundary and Cell are lost. That is not coupling.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Collective Emergence yet.</strong>
						Emergence is a higher-order identity with its own persistence. Coupling is still pairwise or local relation at Interactive scale.
						See physics-lens <a href="/framework/emergent" class="text-white/80 underline decoration-white/25 hover:decoration-white/50">Emergence</a>.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-rose-400/30 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Not Ownership of the partner.</strong>
						A coupled Cell keeps its own jurisdiction. Coupling is relation under distinctness.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Order in the biology lens</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">Interactive complete</h2>
				<ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-3 text-lg">
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Signal</strong> — elementary exchange event</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Recognition</strong> — classify and admit or refuse</li>
					<li><strong class="text-white/85">Coupling</strong> — sustained link under preserved boundaries</li>
				</ol>
				<p>
					<strong class="text-white/85">Next scale (Collective):</strong>
					Multicellularity → Specialization → Regulation,
					when many couplings stabilize into a higher-order living system.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16 border-b border-white/10">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/60 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Engineering</div>
				<h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">What we work on</h2>
				<ul class="space-y-5 text-lg">
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Build links that leave both forms intact:</strong> relation without capture.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Prefer repeated recognized exchange over forced merger:</strong> coupling is earned stability.
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Name the channel:</strong> what actually holds the relation (practice, contract, shared context, technical interface)?
					</li>
					<li class="border-l border-white/15 pl-5">
						<strong class="text-white/85">Watch for scale jump:</strong> when couplings densify into a whole with its own persistence, you are entering Collective, not still pairwise Interactive.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-8 py-16">
			<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-6 text-white/55 leading-relaxed">
				<div class="rounded-2xl border border-cyan-400/20 bg-cyan-400/[0.04] p-6 text-base">
					<div class="mb-2 text-sm uppercase tracking-[3px] text-cyan-300/80">Science reading</div>
					<p>
						Primary discipline: <strong class="text-white/80">cell adhesion / intercellular junctions / stable coupling</strong>.
						Interactive biology-lens set is complete. Collective scale (Multicellularity, Specialization, Regulation) is next when we continue.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 pt-4">
					<a href="/framework/signal" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Signal</a>
					<a href="/framework/recognition" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Recognition</a>
					<a href="/framework/living-identity" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full border border-white/20 text-white/70 hover:bg-white/5 transition">Living Identity</a>
					<a href="/framework" class="px-6 py-3 rounded-full bg-white text-black font-medium hover:bg-white/90 transition">Framework</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
